framework DecisionAudit

domain PostdueContract:
  description "Focused review of the actionable schedule-alert contract"

problem P1:
  "Can POSTDUE and POSTDUE_FORECAST remain warning-only, deterministic, actionable, and shared without adding another DSL or deadline evaluator?"

step S1:
  evidence EV1:
    "The integrated temporal specification is already the sole Grammar 8 authority and defines deadline and latest targets, required and forward schedules, two closed alert kinds, and one shared evaluator"
    resource:
      file "docs/specs/temporal-schedule.md"
      label "Single normative temporal contract"

step S2:
  evidence EV2:
    "Current lateness uses only an incomplete comparable event strictly after its target, while forecast lateness prefers precedence proof over an optimal-false resource heuristic and equality is never late"
    resource:
      file "test/fixtures/postdue-contract-v1.json"
      label "Strict alert and proof cases"

step S3:
  evidence EV3:
    "Project-finish alerts reuse applicable critical paths and intermediate alerts use a target predecessor cone; missing full evidence remains explicitly not-computed or unavailable with exact argv"
    resource:
      file "test/fixtures/postdue-contract-v1.json"
      label "Actionable driver cases"

step S4:
  evidence EV4:
    "Check, Analysis, and Next own one common bounded alert object while diagnostics, recommendation ranking, start authority, mutations, and adapters retain separate responsibilities"
    resource:
      file "docs/specs/temporal-schedule.md"
      label "Projection and authority boundary"

step S5:
  decision D1 based_on P1, EV1, EV2:
    "Refine Section 11 of the existing single specification instead of adding a competing POSTDUE specification or DSL construct"

step S6:
  decision D2 based_on EV2:
    "Accept strict current and forecast comparison, matching-key suppression, independent deadline and latest targets, and precedence-first proof ordering"

step S7:
  decision D3 based_on EV3:
    "Require a relevant available driver or an explicit bounded recovery state and exact dag analyze argv; never present an unrelated global critical path"

step S8:
  decision D4 based_on EV1, EV4, D1, D2, D3:
    "Accept one internal evaluator and one common projection contract without runtime activation, exit failure, recommendation change, or authority change"

step S9:
  pending PD1:
    "Evaluator implementation, command-specific projection, Grammar 8 and Contract 9 activation, release, remote writes, Issue mutation, and plan advance remain later tasks"
